{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339816-inhuman-6-traits","id":1339816,"title":"Inhuman(6+) traits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-06T06:15:03-07:00","id":1339816,"title":"Inhuman(6+) traits?","content":"Hello everyone! So how should inhuman traits work? <br /> <br /> We all know superhuman Abilities/Attributes do exist, and in theory mages can wield them through EXP and up to 10, but there are few mechanics given.<br /> <br /> Do they have some special roles or just add more dices to related pools? (To be honest the latter is very boring...)<br /> <br /> Resources I know:<br /> 1. Revised has Legendary Attributes merit, which also tells you Stamina 6 has some additional functions(soak agg damage)<br /> 2. Mummy Revised lists all Lv.6-8 Attributes<br /> 3. Masters of the Art allows you to have 6 dots if you achieve archmagedom<br /> 4. Some Dark Age books have brief description of 6 dots","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T11:20:20-07:00","id":1339877,"title":"","content":"My taking on this is that attributes-skills above 4 should have special effects, attributes-skills above 6 should have even further effects, though there is a danger games might turn complicated.<br /> In my mind anything above 5 is alien/ottherworldly and scary, stats and rules may not be enough to represent this. It probably should be more of a story element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T11:36:32-07:00","id":1339878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339816-inhuman-6-traits?p=1339877#post1339877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My taking on this is that attributes-skills above 4 should have special effects, attributes-skills above 6 should have even further effects, though there is a danger games might turn complicated.<br /> In my mind anything above 5 is alien/ottherworldly and scary, stats and rules may not be enough to represent this. It probably should be more of a story element.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. And generally speaking 3 dots in traits are excellent to most people, 4 dots are extremely rare, 5 dots is the peak of WHOLE humankind/splat, 6+ are inhuman. So 5 dots and inhuman traits should be very, very rare even if it\u2019s possible.<br /> <br /> Btw to be honest WW authorities do not obey their own rules, especially for vampires. MOST low gens NPCs have insane stats(lots of 6+), which is confirmed by someone that do not follow official creation rules AT ALL. Mages are better, many 4 or 5 dots at most, NPCs having inhumans are countable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 10-06-2019, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T13:13:09-07:00","id":1339893,"title":"","content":"Personally I hate how Mage in earlier additions had Archmages achieve higher traits because each sphere is linked to an Attribute so Archmages only could become inhumane in their Archspheres' tied attribute.<br /> <br /> How I do it is like how Mummies and Wan Gui grow stronger than mortal limits. I simply have Arete be the limit to Traits. For me its treated as significant to have high Arete,even Arete 4 displays a degree of enlightenment you would take note of. Arete 6 Opens the options up for you, you won't necessarily develop inhuman traits though, not everyone is smart because they want to be.<br /> <br /> I also think I will permit Legendary Attributes because it is fun and a simple way to explain Herculean and Genius mages right off the bat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T13:44:02-07:00","id":1339902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339816-inhuman-6-traits#post1339816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone! So how should inhuman traits work?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a need to have them work any different than the simple baseline of having extremely large dice-pools compared to what normal folks can hope to achieve.<br /> <br /> VtM, which has the easiest access to such efforts, never feels lacking because getting your Strength to 6 doesn't have any bonuses that's not inherent in having Strength 6 (keeping in mind that in pre-V5, any vampire could boost their physical Attributes to 6 for the scene if they want to spend the blood for it). If anything having automatic boosts feels like it infringes as the actual supernatural powers like Potence, or worse stacks with Potence is stupidly powerful ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We all know superhuman Abilities/Attributes do exist, and in theory mages can wield them through EXP and up to 10, but there are few mechanics given. </div> </div> </div>The default assumption is that mages can't wield them through XP, or up to 10. Mages can boost their stats that high with magic easily enough though, but that has it's own issues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (To be honest the latter is very boring...) </div> </div> </div>Boring, but practical (esp. when pair with Magic Enhancing Abilities). Also... well.. boring is good to me here. I'd rather mages spend their XP on things besides 6+ traits. What makes mages fun and cool to play are all the cool things they do with magic, not pumping up their stats to levels generally reserved for immortal (not just supernatural) characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339816-inhuman-6-traits?p=1339878#post1339878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And generally speaking 3 dots in traits are excellent to most people, 4 dots are extremely rare, 5 dots is the peak of WHOLE humankind/splat, 6+ are inhuman.</div> </div> </div> </div>While not exactly uncommon... this is a pretty drastic overstatement of things.<br /> <br /> 3 dots is above average, not excellent. They're ratings for people that are good enough to stand out in the crowd so they could find employment in a field that relates to that trait. Physical Attributes at 3 and Athletics 3 aren't going to get you into Major League baseball, but you could easily get work in the minors, helping during spring training, or running serious training camps for high-school and college athletes.<br /> <br /> 4 dots aren't &quot;extremely&quot; rare. Keep in mind that almost all starting level supernaturals start with at least one four in an Attribute unless they take a Flaw to the contrary. This is not stated as some sort of inherent boost from becoming a supernatural (though they did do that in the CofD), but that such aptitude goes hand-in-hand with supernatural existence. As well, 4s in Knowledges are given a more concrete benchmark, that means every college professor that's qualified for their job has at least on 4 on their sheet. Every licensed doctor, lawyer that passed the bar, etc. all have 4s in their fields. While taking some fairly large assumptions here, I think it's fair to say around 1 out of every 15 adults has at least one Ability at 4+ based on how the games define these things. It just feels more rare when you spread out all those 4s between all the different Abilities.<br /> <br /> 5 is, indeed, &quot;peak&quot; but nothing in the book describes this as all that rare, esp. because one trait at 5 alone doesn't make you the peak of humanity. A scientist with Intelligence 2 and Science 5 isn't mechanically better than a Scientist with Intelligence 3 and Science 4. The peak of humanity is the Scientist with Intelligence 5 and Science 5 (and lots of additional side traits). And that's for something nice and easy where the game abstracts things out enough that one Attribute and one Ability is enough. If you want to be peak human as playing soccer, you need a lot of Attributes at 5 on top of your Athletics at 5.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, the PCs have ready access to 4s and 5s, because the game wants them to; gatekeeping it behind perceived notions of rarity isn't really the spirit of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Btw to be honest WW authorities do not obey their own rules, especially for vampires. </div> </div> </div>Sure... though there are no official creation rules for NPCs. The NPCs in the books are just stated however the authors felt they should be, because creation rules are for the PCs to keep the group on roughly the same page regarding what's appropriate at start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T21:22:06-07:00","id":1339991,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm not sure why abilities (i.e. skills/talents/knowledges, not Attributes!) above 5 were always behind some supernatural power barrier (Vampire Generation, etc.) instead of the more simple and realistic mechanic of....age. Pure age.<br /> We can presume 5 is as good as a human can get in something in their normal lifetime; Some do it a bit faster, some take most of their life to reach that level. But if you've practiced something for 200 years, gained knowledge in person about a topic for several centuries or simply have performed certain tasks for that long of a time, without the debilitating effects that normally come with very old age, it stands to reason that 6+ is simply a natural progression of you being around that long for it.<br /> <br /> It would make so much sense, and also give any Unaging merit or immortality effects more mechanical flavor than just roleplaying related possibilities. Of course the ST would have to consider if 6+ 'd be logical for a character - a 300 years old Mage that started woodworking 5 years ago won't push to 6+ in a short time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-07-2019, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T22:50:37-07:00","id":1339996,"title":"","content":"Realism-wise, while impossible to prove in humans, education research tends to favor the idea that learning plateaus; that there isn't an infinite potential to continue growing if you had more time to dedicate to something. This is well demonstrated in the physical realm of activity. Genetic and early developmental conditions are going to set your maximum sprint. If I had 1,000 years to hone the perfect sprinting technique without worrying about bodily decline, I'd still never come close to Usain Bolt. I can't train my ratio of muscle group types to get better sprinter muscles. I can't train my frame to be lankier, so I have a naturally slimmer build with a long stride to increase how efficiently I can turn muscle power into speed. Etc.<br /> <br /> A lot of what we perceive as growth after a certain point is horizontal rather than vertical. In game terms, branching out into different Abilities rather than ever increasing one. I could master playing the guitar, but at some point I'll plateau in how far I can ever go in my specific aptitude for performing as a musician (maxing out Performance). The perception of growth is going to come in as I start improving my song writing abilities (Expression), study musical history and theory (Academics), and develop a better understanding of the science of music, acoustics, and how to apply them via sound engineering (Science and Technology). So I would be growing as an artist, even if my guitar playing skills aren't technically getting better.<br /> <br /> A whole other issue is that skills require upkeep (which is a plausible reason why we don't see continued vertical growth). The more you try to improve your skills, the more time you dedicate to practicing and keeping them up to date. At a certain point, there wouldn't be enough time in the day to practice all your training and you'd slowly start to lose skills you don't focus on. The world's best blacksmith can't just stop smithing for a decade and come back and expect to be at the same level they used to be at. They have t constantly practice their skills just to maintain where they are, and then devote even more time in any hopes of improvement, which would preclude also having time to master lots of other stuff.<br /> <br /> From a simplicity perspective, setting everything at 5 is vastly easier than trying to set plateaus in a fair but more natural/realistic fashion. Having a system to set a character's personal plateaus in every trait is a giant pain in the ass for little positive benefit to playing the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T00:32:40-07:00","id":1340001,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but the question then is, what abilities over 5 even *mean*. Especially in knowledges. If higher values in knowledges are not explainable by supernatural age allowing you to gain more of it, what *do* they represent?<br /> <br /> But, on the other topic, regarding the problem of levels of 4-5 being supposedly quite rare in the population...<br /> The core issue is, that there is a disparity between what those dots technically mean vs. the gameplay-mechanics effect they have at the average table.<br /> Even having a 4 instead of a 3 in an attribute or ability is supposed to, as-written, put you leaps and bounds over the other. Heck, I showed that off in my little signature'd thread about what the individual strength dots actually mean.<br /> Game-mechanics wise though, all you get is simply a single additional die, which doesn't even translate to an additional success on average with standard difficulty. And the standard difficulty of 6 is not an 'everyday stuff' difficulty, but more an 'out of the norm for you' difficulty, as-written.<br /> It's that disconnect between the meaning of the higher level vs. the actual mechanics result that give a feeling of 'More dots aren't a big deal' or 'You really need high stats to pull most things off well.'<br /> <br /> Now, I personally think part of that also mostly stems from some STs having fallen into a trap of not giving enough individual value to the resulting successes of a roll, and rarely if ever going below difficulty 6 for even basic tasks. I've been at tables where the outcome of rolls was &quot;Ah, only two successes. Not enough, sorry, you fail!&quot;, while the books actually stress that if you get successes on a roll in the first place, <i>you in some way, shape or form partially succeeded</i>, and that three successes should give you a full blown just-perfectly-as-you-wanted-it result.<br /> Anything above is moving into territory of &quot;Holy shit that was amazing!&quot; and standing ovations.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: Difficulty is supposed to be the dial for controlling how hard something is - especially *lower* difficulties than 6, which get often neglected by STs - not an arbitrary amount of required successes. Except for non-attribute things like Arete rolls of course. And giving more weight to individual successes in the first place also makes rarity of high dots in attributes/abilities more sensible. If you need to spam high amounts of successes to perform basic actions, everybody needs high stats to function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-07-2019, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T02:23:10-07:00","id":1340006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339816-inhuman-6-traits?p=1340001#post1340001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but the question then is, what abilities over 5 even *mean*. Especially in knowledges. If higher values in knowledges are not explainable by supernatural age allowing you to gain more of it, what *do* they represent?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would interpret from the way the game tends to treat this, that they represent minor supernatural insight or ability. Having Melee 6 doesn't just mean you've studying fighting for centuries, it means you've learned how to leverage your supernatural self in combination with weapon based fighting. That's why it's locked behind some level of supernatural power. A vampire needs to be low enough Generation to extend blood buffing to a more passive increase in their ability to weapon a blade. A mage needs enough Arete to recognize the rules of mundane fighting are one more thing to bend slightly. Etc.<br /> <br /> Knowledges would follow the same consideration. Science 6 isn't some wider breadth of knowledge from learning more science facts over the centuries, it's a supernatural ability to piece things together by seeing connections humans can't on their own (or at least not nearly as quickly).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T15:42:04-07:00","id":1340694,"title":"","content":"I don't know about modern era Mage but in DA:Mage I have a system for permanent supernatural stats (but I also require players to spend XP as normal). Three dots in your Fundation and 3 dots in 2 of your relevant Pillars allow you to permanently raise one of your attributes to 6 dots by casting an ongoning extended spell. You need 60 successes gained over 10 minutes intervals. As per the usual rules you also need to spend 1 point of quintessence for success (so 60 quintesence) then another 15 quintessence and 2 willpower points to seal the spell.<br /> <br /> For example an hermetic with Modus 3, Anima 3 and Primus 3 can attempt the ritual above to permanently increase one of his own physical attributes to 6 (provided said attribute was at 5 dots already AND the correct amount of XP was avaiable), while using Corona 3 instead of Anima allows to increase mental attributes and using Forces does the same with social attributes.<br /> <br /> It's costy, but during the DA this does not cause backlash unless you botch. The system is also meant to allow for higher increases (4 dots in fundation, 4 dots in one pillar 3 in the next allow you to attempt a ritual to increase an attribute to 7 and 4 dots in fundation and 4 in 2 relevant pillars allow for an increase to 8 dots, 5 dots in fundation, 5 dots in one pillar and 4 dots in another one and you can try to get one attribute to 9 and finally you need 5 in fundation and 5 in 2 pillars to get 10 permanent dots in one attribute. Obviously the quintessence and willpower expense increases as well, following the rules of ongoning spells).<br /> <br /> I've never considered 6+ abilities raised on a permanent basis but I suppose one could adapt the method above in order to get the desired result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 10-10-2019, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T16:54:36-07:00","id":1340700,"title":"","content":"I find that many people regard Arete as something like Dharma or Generation. It may make some sense because it represents the depth of mage\u2019s understanding. Some books also use this.<br /> <br /> If I use this rules I will make Arete be equal to Dharma, 13 - Arete = mage\u2019s Generation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T10:15:29-08:00","id":1350669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339816-inhuman-6-traits?p=1339893#post1339893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I hate how Mage in earlier additions had Archmages achieve higher traits because each sphere is linked to an Attribute so Archmages only could become inhumane in their Archspheres' tied attribute.<br /> <br /> How I do it is like how Mummies and Wan Gui grow stronger than mortal limits. I simply have Arete be the limit to Traits. For me its treated as significant to have high Arete,even Arete 4 displays a degree of enlightenment you would take note of. Arete 6 Opens the options up for you, you won't necessarily develop inhuman traits though, not everyone is smart because they want to be.<br /> <br /> I also think I will permit Legendary Attributes because it is fun and a simple way to explain Herculean and Genius mages right off the bat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the higher sphere ratings only made your 6+ attributes paradox free<br /> <br /> To have them at all is probably a function of superhuman(6+) Arete. Or that's how i would rule it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T11:08:16-08:00","id":1350677,"title":"","content":"In the sister game <i>Awakening</i>, mages can raise Attributes and Abilities as high as 10 (or a limit of 5 or Gnosis, whichever is higher). Different rules and different there, true. But looking at it objectively as a bunch of descriptive numbers, six to ten is not really *that* superhuman. I have the same issue with old D&amp;D and most superhero games. Allow me to use superheros to illustrate my point. Batman and Captain America, both at peak human potential (say Strength 5). In comparison, what Strength would Superman or the Hulk have? 10? Only twice as strong? I understand thematically it represents much more than that. But in the math mechanics, a Str 10 punch does the same damage as a Str 5 guy with a sword. Superhuman yeah, but just barely.<br /> <br /> Which is to say that, in the role of a st, I would have no issue with a PC raising stats above 5 if they spend the xp and have a plausible excuse. I would not invoke pattern bleeding, as it just seems to be an artificial meta-game barrier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T15:18:17-08:00","id":1350710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339816-inhuman-6-traits?p=1350677#post1350677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But looking at it objectively as a bunch of descriptive numbers, six to ten is not really *that* superhuman.</div> </div> </div> </div>That...reeaaally depends.<br /> In terms of extra dice, at first glance? No, not that much. But then you have to consider that 3 successes at a task already means 'fully achieved perfeclty' and 5 means 'amazing!'.<br /> <br /> Personally I think that the underestimation of successess, and the feeling of higher rating not being too superhuman stems from the combat system, where one's just used to tons of dice in the more combat orentied splats. But if you look at things like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1133404-intersting-facts-about-the-strength-attribute\">the strength attribute</a> or read up on what the actual numbers behind attributes and skills actually *mean*, independant of dice...yeah. 6-10 is definitely superhuman. 6 maaaaaaaybe can be explained away by onlookers, but higher ratings are legitimately crazy.<br /> <br /> And again - it's honestly the combat system that diminishes it through its simplified mechanics (strengh 6 giving you like 0.5 damage more on average, but it literally allows you to lift almost 200 pounds more than 5...) .<br /> Outside of combat, the ratings are a whole different animal- and should be the focus when it comes to superhuman stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-24-2019, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T22:31:50-08:00","id":1350770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339816-inhuman-6-traits#post1339816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Mummy Revised lists all Lv.6-8 Attributes</div> </div> </div> </div> Watch out with this--the special powers or abilities listed for Lvls. 6-8 are incredibly specific to the sorts of powers Mummies (and specifically the Amenti--mummies made using the non-corrupted/actually functioning life equation/immortality spell/Horus magic thing). To get one of the extra powers listed, you have to have boosted that attribute above 5 by specifically using a mummy potion/amulet/spell/whatever. Then, if and only if you used a mummy Haku (Hekau?) power to boost that attribute, you get to pick a SINGLE power (or invent your own using the listed ones for scale) per attribute level above five. Mind you, to use mummy stuff, you don't necessarily have to be a mummy, but you might need True Faith or something. Mummies are basically good incarnate. I mean, I'd pick up the book to see all the parameters--but I will note that 99.9% of Mages aren't using those loots out of the box. You can house rule it and say that some mages can, or whatever (you can house rule anything obviously,) but just be cognizant that, as the game exists right now, those powers for attributes above 5 that are listed in Mummy: The Resurrection have a very limited scope and availability.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T10:37:41-08:00","id":1350853,"title":"","content":"I was thinking reading this about how 5+ does exponentially increase in capacity but then I realized what folks were saying about the mechanical-narrative disconnect and I have to agree given that mechanically it really is a linear increase from the realms of 6-10, when it should be far more impressive.<br /> <br /> All I can think is maybe taking something from 1e Scion, loath as I am to admit it could be useful here. Perhaps increasing the bonus exponentially from 6-10. Say if 6 provided 2 bonus dice after 5 instead of one, 7 provided 4 bonus dice after 5 instead of two, 8 provided 8 bonus dice after 5 instead of three, etc.<br /> <br /> Then again, I've never claimed to be that great at crunch, so I have no idea if that would work, but it's an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T13:46:26-08:00","id":1350901,"title":"","content":"I kinda like the way they did it in the original Aberrant with Mega Attributes. You had the regular trait 1 to 5, and then a Mega trait 1 to 5 attached to it. The mega attribute could add dice OR reduce the difficulty, or a bit of both. At low scores more dice are better. But once you are at 5 dice or so, reducing Difficulty is far more potent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T14:02:46-08:00","id":1350905,"title":"","content":"If we're going to talk about those games... Trinity/Scion 2e handles that much better in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T03:49:49-07:00","id":1405775,"title":"","content":"I feel like you should be able to play off level 6th strength and especially stamina as coincidental.<br /> <br /> If a 5 foot, 100 pound mother can lift a car off her child because she's hyped up on adrenaline, a larger much more muscular man can make the same claim in other extreme circumstances. As for stamina, people have survived skydiving and having their parachutes fail. They just landed just right. It's amazing the extreme variance in what can kill a healthy person, with one dying from a simple slip on the ice, while another person, seemingly no more healthy than the first manages to survive being hit by a bus or being thrown out the window of car flipping over at high speeds.<br /> <br /> Now jacking up all your physical stats to 9 and fist fighting a Brujah is not going to fly, but a 6, I think that should be able to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T11:59:44-07:00","id":1405817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339816-inhuman-6-traits?p=1405775#post1405775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like you should be able to play off level 6th strength and especially stamina as coincidental.If a 5 foot, 100 pound mother can lift a car off her child because she's hyped up on adrenaline, a larger much more muscular man can make the same claim in other extreme circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>The WoD rules actually cover this - the lifting rules have a set series of values, but you can actually jump *up* levels if you succeed on a diff 9 willpower roll.<br /> <br /> So yeah, strength 6 lifting *can* pass as 'omg wow!' but nothing supernatural per se - if you don't do it day in and out because you are bored.<br /> The Legendary Attribute merit does not cause paradox and allows you to push to 6, but it is quite special - and probably has to be used in moderation for certain physical feats or people *will* want to study you (non-sinisterly) to see what makes you tick.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T15:22:08-07:00","id":1405841,"title":"","content":"It's also worth remembering that the &quot;mother flips a car off their child,&quot; is more myth than reality. The reality is usually, &quot;mother lifts a car a few inches for just long enough for their child to not be pinned, and then goes to the hospital from all the harm that strain did to her body.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a reason our bodies gate off our full potential strength behind emergency responses: exercising it can do serious harm to our bodies and that risk needs to be weighed against the action in question.<br /> <br /> Even if you overcame the physiological barriers somehow to get to the equivalent of Strength 6, for a &quot;normal&quot; human the strain would at a minimum permanently reduce their Stamina and maximum Stamina by 1 to represent the huge strain we're talking about. There are just limits on human biology where trade offs set in, and improving one part of your body is going to start negatively impacting other parts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T15:45:56-07:00","id":1405845,"title":"","content":"Doesn't matter if it's more myth than reality; it's a common enough belief to render acts of Magick patterned after it Coincidental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T02:54:21-07:00","id":1405901,"title":"","content":"OK... so if you want to say that burst of strength in high stress situations is coincidental, that's fine. That's not the same thing as permanently having Strength 6. The myth isn't, &quot;your child is trapped under a car, and after the surge of effort to rescue them, you become Captain America.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T06:55:03-07:00","id":1405937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339816-inhuman-6-traits#post1339816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone! So how should inhuman traits work?<br /> <br /> We all know superhuman Abilities/Attributes do exist, and in theory mages can wield them through EXP and up to 10, but there are few mechanics given.<br /> <br /> Do they have some special roles or just add more dices to related pools? (To be honest the latter is very boring...)<br /> <br /> Resources I know:<br /> 1. Revised has Legendary Attributes merit, which also tells you Stamina 6 has some additional functions(soak agg damage)<br /> 2. Mummy Revised lists all Lv.6-8 Attributes<br /> 3. Masters of the Art allows you to have 6 dots if you achieve archmagedom<br /> 4. Some Dark Age books have brief description of 6 dots</div> </div> </div> </div>I was a fan of having Arete determine your stat cap rather then Spheres, much like how Dharma and Balance does it for Vampires and Mummies. I'm a fan of this type of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T12:59:51-07:00","id":1405982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339816-inhuman-6-traits?p=1405775#post1405775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like you should be able to play off level 6th strength and especially stamina as coincidental.<br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Temporary Dexterity 6 (or even 7 or 8) could also be Coincidental, considering how mass media have popularized humans being capable of amazing feats. Likewise with Mental or Social attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-02-2020, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T13:19:43-07:00","id":1405985,"title":"","content":"Temporary attributes is all Magick can do unless you engage in extending the Duration or turning the enhanced person into a Relic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T14:23:42-07:00","id":1405997,"title":"","content":"Inhuman attributes and how they react to others should depend entirely upon how you got them; Vampires? You look the same as you did upon the embrace even if you gained five dots since then (I Forget if blood buffing had visible signs or not) Investment? , even the less malicious demons are gonna give you some strange paradox-like effects. Mage trick? Ditto. Genuine human enlightenment? That has the potential of being all benefits. <br /> <br /> You can <i>perfectly </i>achieve a 9 in your physical, social or mental rating through enlightenment, or you can get messy with magic(k)al improvements. Let's say... you could increase the size of the soul or you could add something onto it, the former being superior to the latter. A Mage is capable of both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}